+/// A front end for a language lowered to C may show its declarations in debug
+/// info as the source wrote them: a name inside modules, `a::b::f`, becomes
+/// the name `f` in the namespaces `a` and `b`, as C++ would write it. Asked
+/// for each function, variable, typedef and tag whose debug info is made;
+/// returns true and sets \param Scope (`a::b`) and \param Name (`f`) to
+/// replace what clang would use, or false to keep it. Null (the default)
+/// changes nothing.
+#define CLANG_HAS_DEBUG_NAME_HOOK 1
+extern bool (*DebugNameHook)(const NamedDecl *D, std::string &Scope,
+                             std::string &Name);
